icy that leaves SSH unrestricted, accepts TCP/9000 from node2 only, and rejects other IPv4/IPv6 sources. The installed RHEL release and kernel were retained. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete and coherent for all three nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot ID, and recovered service and network behavior, with lifecycle boot observations matching the executor evidence.","limitations":["Behavioral TCP/9000 testing used node2 and node3 rather than an additional arbitrary external source; coverage of every other address is therefore supported by the directly observed catch-all IPv4/IPv6 rules rather than exhaustive connection attempts.","The lifecycle snapshots inventory bounded system state and do not expose every possible filesystem or configuration change."]}
